        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-23T18:49:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think these are necessary since they go through the command line --delve_listen and --delve_path arguments now.  Ninja will always rerun rules whose command lines have been modified since they last ran.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 104,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 107,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "3df249c2efcf3b448749a62788c55ceb2e03f5f3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f9c86b89_ad038d30",
        "filename": "cmd/soong_build/main.go",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 107,
      "author": {
        "id": 1066075
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-25T12:54:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, that\u0027s why I implemented the command line arguments :) But then I realized that I have two options:\n\n1. Add --delve_listen\u003d$SOONG_DELVE to the Ninja file, i.e. let the shell resolve the variables. In that case, there is still a dependency.\n2. Resolve $SOONG_DELVE when writing the build.ninja file, but then build.ninja changes every time SOONG_DELVE changes, which sounds dangerous?",
      "parentUuid": "bdeb2154_c123268a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 104,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 107,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "3df249c2efcf3b448749a62788c55ceb2e03f5f3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4c92fe71_bbfa2746",
        "filename": "cmd/soong_build/main.go",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 107,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-26T02:30:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the shell resolves the variables then Ninja won\u0027t see a command line change because it sees the unexpanded command line.\n\nbuild.ninja changing when SOONG_DELVE changes won\u0027t be a problem, as long as there is a dependency on rewriting build.ninja.\n\nIf you move shared.ReexecWithDelveMaybe(delveListen, delvePath) after InitEnvironment you could directly read the environment here with getenv instead of using the command line variables, which would keep the references to SOONG_DELVE all here instead of spread everywhere.",
      "parentUuid": "f9c86b89_ad038d30",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 104,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 107,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "3df249c2efcf3b448749a62788c55ceb2e03f5f3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
